  "name": "Gurna (Tupuri song-dance society)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song-dance society of the Tupuri of the Mayo-Danay in Cameroon and the Mayo-Kebbi in Chad. Men gather in dry-season camps, where composers create new songs that the group then performs in large circle dances; the songs praise, criticise and comment on village life, as James Ignatowski's ethnography Journey of Song describes. Charles Duvelle recorded Tupuri songs in 1966. The voice card, set to a live group, carries the massed singing.",
